          "query": "from(bucket: \"puit\")\n  |> range(start: v.timeRangeStart, stop: v.timeRangeStop)\n  |> filter(fn: (r) => r._measurement == \"pump_volume\")\n  |> filter(fn: (r) => r._field == \"volume_l\" or r._field == \"volume_sigma_l\"\n                    or r._field == \"rate_l_per_h\" or r._field == \"duration_s\"\n                    or r._field == \"quality\")\n  // No keep()/group() before the pivot. quality is a STRING field and the rest are\n  // floats; folding them into one _value column is a type collision Flux rejects at\n  // query time. pivot drops _field from the group key by itself, which merges the\n  // field tables into one row per run with each field keeping its own column type.\n  // quality is a field and not a tag so that rechecking a run overwrites it rather\n  // than adding a second series beside it.\n  |> pivot(rowKey: [\"_time\"], columnKey: [\"_field\"], valueColumn: \"_value\")\n  |> sort(columns: [\"_time\"])\n  |> tail(n: 3)",
